# Workflow

- Read `docs/agents/LEARNINGS.md`, then pick exactly one task id from `docs/TASKS.md`.
- Read that task's REQ ids in `docs/REQUIREMENTS.md` before writing code.
- TDD: add failing tests, make them pass, then refactor. Do not start with the implementation.
- Keep the pull request scoped to that task. Tick only your own line in `docs/TASKS.md`.
- Run `pnpm check` before pushing. If CI fails, fix it on the same branch until it is green.
- Never skip or disable a test or lint rule to get green. Never lower a coverage threshold. Never commit secrets.
- Code, comments, and commit messages are English. User-facing CLI messages are Spanish. Error codes stay stable identifiers (`E_…`, `W_…`).
- Append a dated line to `docs/agents/LEARNINGS.md` when you hit a new pitfall.
